                <pb facs="0102" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg90"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.20/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-15T10:00:00-06:00">July 15, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. Department’s telegram No. 63, July 12, 5 p.m. The Legation has now received
                    the formal written request of the Government of Costa Rica for the detail of the
                    military mission and requesting to know the terms upon which it would be sent.
                    The Government requests reply at the earliest possible date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hornibrook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
